# livediagram MCP server (docs/specs/015-api/mcp-server.md). No secrets live here: the MCP forwards the
# caller's Bearer lwt_ token to the api worker over a service binding, and the
# OAuth consent + token mint authenticate via the signed-in session in
# apps/editor + apps/api.
#
# Configure via wrangler, not env vars:
#   - the API service binding (apps/api) — see wrangler.toml
#   - the OAUTH_KV namespace: `wrangler kv namespace create OAUTH_KV`, then put
#     the id in wrangler.toml
#
# Optional [vars] (wrangler.toml or `wrangler secret put`):
#   - CONSENT_BASE_URL: origin of the live app that serves the OAuth consent
#     page (`/oauth/consent`). Defaults to https://livediagram.app, so a
#     a deployment serving the editor on its own domain must point this at that
#     origin or OAuth callers land on the hosted consent screen instead.
#     Every tool's document and share links are built on it too.
# CONSENT_BASE_URL=https://livediagram.app
#   - TELEMETRY_KEY: livediagram's secret (a worker secret) on the liveworkspace
#     telemetry service (docs/specs/017-telemetry/telemetry.md), the SAME value as
#     the api worker's. Unset = this worker sends no telemetry, so it is safe
#     to skip on a deployment.
# TELEMETRY_KEY=<random string>
#   - TELEMETRY_URL: the service. Unset means https://www.liveworkspace.app/api/telemetry.
# TELEMETRY_URL=http://localhost:8790/api/telemetry
#
# The MCP is gated on auth being enabled end-to-end: with sign-in unset, the
# api's /api/oauth/exchange rejects every caller and the consent page has no
# signed-in user, so no token can be minted (docs/specs/015-api/mcp-server.md §3.7). A no-auth
# a deployment simply doesn't deploy this worker.
